# Netlify _headers file
# https://docs.netlify.com/routing/headers/
#
# Goal: stop re-downloading the full page/JS/CSS on every visit.
# - HTML pages: always revalidate (so users get new deploys promptly),
#   but "must-revalidate" lets the browser send a conditional request
#   (If-None-Match) and get a tiny 304 back instead of the full file
#   when nothing changed.
# - styles.css / hub.js / app.js: same conditional-revalidate approach.
#   NOTE: bump the CACHE_VERSION in sw.js on every deploy that changes
#   these, since the filenames themselves aren't content-hashed.
# - Icons and the manifest: these basically never change once shipped,
#   so cache them for a full year.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/hub.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
